  "title": "The Minimum 2-Circuit Decomposition of an 18-Triangle Torus",
  "batch_label": "61",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For the fixed 18-facet triangulated torus S defined verbatim in source.md and precisely interpreted in problem.md, the minimum number of 2-circuits in a facet-exact 2-circuit decomposition is c(S)=3. The cyclic words 105374, 216587, and 023648 form a minimum decomposition. Modulo cyclic rotation and reversal of individual circuits and permutation of circuits, there are exactly three labeled minimum decompositions; the automorphism group Aut(S) has order 108 and is transitive on them, so there is exactly one minimum-decomposition orbit after also quotienting by Aut(S).",
